From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marcel Ritter <marcel@linux-ng.de>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:31:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [core,peer] deny a client's Shutdown Request once the session
 runs

A client that wants to close the connection may first send a Shutdown
Request PDU ([MS-RDPBCGR] 2.2.2.2); mstsc does so when the user clicks
the X in its connection bar. [MS-RDPBCGR] 1.3.1.4.1: if a logged-on
user account is associated with the session, the server always denies
the request with a Shutdown Request Denied PDU (2.2.2.3); the client
then sends a Disconnect Provider Ultimatum with reason "user
requested" and closes the connection itself. Only without a logged-on
user does the server close the connection at once.

peer_recv_data_pdu() always took the second path: it sent a
Disconnect Provider Ultimatum with reason "provider initiated" and
quit. To mstsc that is the server ending a session it asked to leave
cleanly. In the field, the next connection from the same mstsc
process did not show what the server drew while the login waited
(a second factor), until mstsc was restarted.

Once PostConnect has accepted the client (client->connected), answer
with a Shutdown Request Denied PDU and keep the connection; the
client's Disconnect Provider Ultimatum ends it as before. Before that
(PostConnect running or not yet reached: no session) the connection
is closed at once, as until now.
---
 libfreerdp/core/peer.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libfreerdp/core/peer.c b/libfreerdp/core/peer.c
index d8e8595..af65a56 100644
--- a/libfreerdp/core/peer.c
+++ b/libfreerdp/core/peer.c
@@ -327,6 +327,19 @@ static BOOL freerdp_peer_check_fds(freerdp_peer* peer)
 	return (status >= 0);
 }
 
+/* [MS-RDPBCGR] 2.2.2.3 Server Shutdown Request Denied PDU: a Share Data Header only. */
+WINPR_ATTR_NODISCARD
+static BOOL rdp_send_server_shutdown_denied_pdu(rdpRdp* rdp)
+{
+	UINT16 sec_flags = 0;
+	wStream* s = rdp_data_pdu_init(rdp, &sec_flags);
+	if (!s)
+		return FALSE;
+
+	WINPR_ASSERT(rdp->mcs);
+	return rdp_send_data_pdu(rdp, s, DATA_PDU_TYPE_SHUTDOWN_DENIED, rdp->mcs->userId, sec_flags);
+}
+
 static state_run_t peer_recv_data_pdu(freerdp_peer* client, wStream* s,
                                       WINPR_ATTR_UNUSED UINT16 totalLength)
 {
@@ -388,6 +401,17 @@ static state_run_t peer_recv_data_pdu(freerdp_peer* client, wStream* s,
 			return STATE_RUN_CONTINUE; // State changed, trigger rerun
 
 		case DATA_PDU_TYPE_SHUTDOWN_REQUEST:
+			/* [MS-RDPBCGR] 1.3.1.4.1: with a logged-on user (here: PostConnect accepted the
+			 * client) the server always denies, and the client ends the connection itself
+			 * with a "user requested" Disconnect Provider Ultimatum. Without one the server
+			 * closes the connection at once. */
+			if (client->connected)
+			{
+				if (!rdp_send_server_shutdown_denied_pdu(rdp))
+					return STATE_RUN_FAILED;
+				WLog_DBG(TAG, "shutdown request denied, the client disconnects itself");
+				break;
+			}
 			mcs_send_disconnect_provider_ultimatum(rdp->mcs,
 			                                       Disconnect_Ultimatum_provider_initiated);
 			WLog_WARN(TAG, "disconnect provider ultimatum sent to peer, closing connection");
